Additional Use Grant

1. Production use. You may make production use of the Licensed Work free of
   charge unless the Consolidated Revenue of your Corporate Group for its most
   recently completed fiscal year exceeded one hundred million United States
   dollars (USD 100,000,000). Above that amount, production use requires a
   separate commercial license from the Licensor.

2. Non-production use. Non-production use — including evaluation, development,
   testing, research, teaching, and personal use — is free of charge for
   everyone, regardless of size.

3. Public-interest use. Use by a registered nonprofit organization, an
   educational institution, or a public-sector body acting in its public
   capacity is free of charge, regardless of size.

4. Output. Any artifact that the Licensed Work produces, processes, compiles,
   emits, or otherwise operates on — including source code, binaries,
   packages, documents, reports, hardware descriptions, and deployed services
   — is yours. Such output does not become a derivative work of the Licensed
   Work merely by being produced with it, is not subject to this License, and
   carries no obligation to the Licensor. Where the Licensed Work
   intentionally embeds Licensor-owned runtime or support material into its
   output, that embedded material is granted to you under the MIT license (see
   LICENSES/MIT.txt).

5. Attribution of use. Production use of the Licensed Work carried out on
   behalf of another party — for example by a contractor, agency, or
   consultant — is attributed to the party for whom it is carried out, and
   that party's Corporate Group determines whether paragraph 1 applies.
   Conversely, a party that merely uses a service, product, or output of
   another party who used the Licensed Work is not itself a user of the
   Licensed Work by reason of that use alone.

6. Definitions. "Corporate Group" means you together with every entity that
   controls you, that you control, or that is under common control with you,
   where control means the direct or indirect power to direct the management
   and policies of an entity, determined on the same basis of consolidation
   that applies to that group's own financial statements. "Consolidated
   Revenue" means the gross revenue of that Corporate Group as reported in its
   audited or filed consolidated financial statements for the relevant fiscal
   year, converted to United States dollars at the rate that group itself
   applied in those statements. "Production use" means any use other than
   evaluation, development, testing, research, teaching, or personal use.

